@meta
id: 06-12
title: The fourth comma, in three keys
chapter: 06
type: lesson
skills: find-f, line-start
par: 55
minutes: 5
vscode: count the commas with your finger on the screen
open: orders.csv

@brief
A CSV export needs a new `channel` column inserted between `currency` and
`status`, with the value `web` on every data row:

    order,customer,amount,currency,channel,status,placed_at

The header and both rows have the same shape, so the insert point is the
same in all three: immediately before the fourth comma.

`f,` finds the first comma. You want the fourth, and you do not want to
press `f,` four times.

@keys
| `4f,` | forward to the fourth comma on this line |
| `3f(` | forward to the third open paren |
| `0` | column one |

@hints
Counts work in front of `f` exactly as they worked in front of `j` in
chapter 4.
--
`4f,` takes you to the fourth comma in three keystrokes. Then `i` puts your
text in front of it.
--
Start each row with `0`. After an insert the cursor is somewhere in the
middle of the line, and `f` counts from wherever the cursor is — not from
the start of the line.

@solution
    4f, i ,channel <Esc> j 0 4f, i ,web <Esc> j 0 4f, i ,web <Esc> :wq<Enter>

Counting commas with your eyes is slow and wrong about one time in ten.
Counting them with a keystroke is instant and wrong never — and if you do
miscount, `u` and a different count fixes it in two keys.

Note what the count is doing. `4f,` does not mean go four commas further, it
means go to the fourth comma from here. That is why the `0` at the start of
each row matters: the count is only meaningful relative to a position you
know. Anchor, count, land, edit.

This is the shape of nearly all precise work in a delimited line — CSV rows,
argument lists, long type literals. The field you want is the nth something,
and a three-key motion gets you there while the mouse is still travelling.

@start orders.csv
order,customer,amount,currency,status,placed_at
ord_1042,cus_88,4999,GBP,CANCELLED,2024-03-11
ord_1043,cus_91,1250,GBP,PENDING,2024-03-12

@expected orders.csv
order,customer,amount,currency,channel,status,placed_at
ord_1042,cus_88,4999,GBP,web,CANCELLED,2024-03-11
ord_1043,cus_91,1250,GBP,web,PENDING,2024-03-12
